# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND on checkout.
#
# Not cosmetic. Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) checks text files out
# as CRLF, and a bash script with CRLF line endings fails on Linux with the
# useless message `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` -- so build.sh, test_runner.sh
# and import_check.sh, which README.md tells Linux users to run directly, would
# be broken for anyone who cloned on Windows and shared the tree, or who checked
# out on Linux from a Windows-normalised commit.
#
# eol=lf (not just text=auto) is what forces the working-copy ending too.
# PowerShell, Godot and every tool in this project read LF fine on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where it is load-bearing rather than tidy.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.gd   text eol=lf
*.tscn text eol=lf
*.cfg  text eol=lf
*.godot text eol=lf

# Never touch these -- the GodotSteam addon ships prebuilt binaries for every
# platform, and a line-ending "fix" applied to one corrupts it silently.
*.dll    binary
*.so     binary
*.dylib  binary
*.exe    binary
*.bin    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.wav    binary
*.glb    binary
